  "prompt": "Explain the fundamental difference in how location-based AR systems and superimposition-based AR systems determine where and what digital content to display.",
  "reference_answer": "Location-based applications rely on sensors, such as GPS, to detect the user's location with respect to a reference frame. The digital content is then augmented based on that specific location provided by the sensor. Conversely, superimposition-based applications use computer vision techniques to recognize objects in the physical world. Once an object is detected, digital content can be augmented depending on that recognition, allowing the system to superimpose content onto the real-world scene.",
