  "reference_answer": "The graphics pipeline begins by converting scene surfaces into triangular meshes, which are then sent to the GPU. The GPU first performs modeling transformations on the vertices, simultaneously transforming multiple vertices using the same matrix. Next, the stream of triangles is projected onto the view plane, resulting in device coordinates. In the rasterization stage, the GPU exploits inherent parallelism by treating each pixel independently to determine its color. Finally, during pixel processing, GPUs use high-speed memory for surface texturing and employ the depth buffer algorithm for hidden surface removal.",
