  "reference_answer": "The primary difference lies in the objective and the constraints applied. The Optimal Tour approach aims to find a path that covers all vertices in a given graph while traversing it in minimum time. Conversely, the POI maximization approach imposes a time constraint and seeks to find a path that covers the maximum number of POIs within that threshold. While both methods seek an optimal path, the POI approach acknowledges that it is not mandatory to visit every single node, unlike the previous approach. Therefore, the Optimal Tour is used when covering all points is critical, whereas the POI maximization is used when time limits are strict and maximizing exposure is the priority.",
