  "reference_answer": "The core challenge is that the initial graph is not assumed to be complete, meaning some vertices lack direct connections. To address this, a hypothetical edge is introduced between any two vertices that are not directly connected. The length of this hypothetical edge is not a simple Euclidean distance, but rather the shortest path length between those two vertices. This shortest path length is calculated by summing the edge weights along the shortest route. By implementing this modified edge weight definition, we create a new graph that is a valid instance of the TSP, allowing us to find the optimum path.",
